1
00:00:01,875 --> 00:00:03,583
[♪♪♪]

2
00:00:04,333 --> 00:00:07,416
[Nya] I can't believe
we're finally together, Jay.

3
00:00:07,416 --> 00:00:11,000
[Kai] The team wasn't the same
without you, buddy.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,916
[♪♪♪]

5
00:00:16,041 --> 00:00:18,750
[♪♪♪]

6
00:00:23,583 --> 00:00:25,416
[Nya] Too bad you're a failure.

7
00:00:25,416 --> 00:00:26,375
What did you say?

8
00:00:26,375 --> 00:00:29,500
I said, you are a failure.

9
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,541
I placed my faith in you
for nothing.

10
00:00:32,541 --> 00:00:34,791
You said you could capture Ras.

11
00:00:34,791 --> 00:00:37,833
The only thing you've caught
is feelings.

12
00:00:37,833 --> 00:00:40,458
[♪♪♪]

13
00:00:40,458 --> 00:00:42,250
Face it, old man.

14
00:00:42,250 --> 00:00:44,333
Even if you were once a Ninja,

15
00:00:44,333 --> 00:00:45,958
you've fallen too far

16
00:00:45,958 --> 00:00:48,125
for them to ever take you back.

17
00:00:48,125 --> 00:00:49,166
[gasping] Uh...

18
00:00:49,166 --> 00:00:50,708
uh... stay back!

19
00:00:50,708 --> 00:00:53,583
You're one of us, Jay,
not them.

20
00:00:55,083 --> 00:00:56,125
Aah!

21
00:01:00,791 --> 00:01:03,500
[♪♪♪]

22
00:01:04,791 --> 00:01:06,541
[gasping]

23
00:01:07,625 --> 00:01:10,708
[gasping]

24
00:01:11,791 --> 00:01:13,458
Meditation didn't go well?

25
00:01:13,458 --> 00:01:14,458
[sighing]

26
00:01:14,458 --> 00:01:16,291
Didn't find any answers,

27
00:01:16,291 --> 00:01:17,958
if that's what you're asking.

28
00:01:17,958 --> 00:01:19,416
Just confusion.

29
00:01:19,416 --> 00:01:21,583
You sure I did this
all the time?

30
00:01:21,583 --> 00:01:23,000
Seems boring.

31
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:24,166
[sighing]

32
00:01:24,166 --> 00:01:25,208
You did.

33
00:01:25,208 --> 00:01:26,625
You didn't always like it,

34
00:01:26,625 --> 00:01:29,000
but meditation's part of
being a Ninja.

35
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,375
It doesn't just
hand you clear answers,

36
00:01:31,375 --> 00:01:33,250
but it can process bad thoughts

37
00:01:33,250 --> 00:01:35,125
to make room for better ones.

38
00:01:35,125 --> 00:01:37,916
Those weren't
better thoughts, trust me.

39
00:01:37,916 --> 00:01:39,333
[sighing]

40
00:01:39,333 --> 00:01:40,625
Life without memories

41
00:01:40,625 --> 00:01:44,291
is like
feeling around in the dark.

42
00:01:45,666 --> 00:01:47,750
[Kai] Ugh,
I can't meditate either.

43
00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:50,166
It's like I can't hold
a thought in this place.

44
00:01:50,166 --> 00:01:51,375
I don't like it here.

45
00:01:51,375 --> 00:01:52,541
We should go.

46
00:01:52,541 --> 00:01:54,375
We planned to stay til dawn,

47
00:01:54,375 --> 00:01:56,458
but the sun
should be up by now,

48
00:01:56,458 --> 00:01:58,500
and I don't want to wait
any longer.

49
00:01:58,500 --> 00:02:00,541
We need to figure out
how to get home.

50
00:02:00,541 --> 00:02:01,916
I'll light the way.

51
00:02:01,916 --> 00:02:03,000
[sputtering]

52
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:04,166
Dang it.

53
00:02:04,166 --> 00:02:07,000
Keep forgetting our powers
are on the fritz.

54
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:10,458
This situation
just keeps getting better.

55
00:02:10,458 --> 00:02:12,750
[♪♪♪]

56
00:02:13,875 --> 00:02:15,125
Ooh! [gasping] What the--?

57
00:02:18,166 --> 00:02:21,083
Who needs powers?

58
00:02:23,291 --> 00:02:24,791
[♪♪♪]

59
00:02:26,333 --> 00:02:28,583
I feel better already.
[laughing awkwardly]

60
00:02:28,583 --> 00:02:29,750
Sarcasm.

61
00:02:29,750 --> 00:02:31,666
Why is the ground all squishy?

62
00:02:31,666 --> 00:02:33,833
[squelching]

63
00:02:36,291 --> 00:02:37,416
What is that?

64
00:02:40,500 --> 00:02:42,875
Is the sky... moving?

65
00:02:42,875 --> 00:02:44,791
Not the sky,

66
00:02:44,791 --> 00:02:46,750
those things!

67
00:02:46,750 --> 00:02:47,791
[snarling]

68
00:02:47,791 --> 00:02:49,750
♪ Lost in the unknown ♪

69
00:02:49,750 --> 00:02:50,916
♪ So much to see ♪

70
00:02:50,916 --> 00:02:54,458
♪ Jump up, kick back
whip around and spin ♪

71
00:02:54,458 --> 00:02:55,791
♪ Together we will rise ♪

72
00:02:55,791 --> 00:02:57,083
♪ Whip around and spin ♪

73
00:02:57,083 --> 00:02:58,708
♪ Together we will rise ♪

74
00:02:58,708 --> 00:03:00,375
♪ For what's right ♪

75
00:03:05,875 --> 00:03:07,041
[Lloyd] I'm sorry,

76
00:03:07,041 --> 00:03:10,500
there must be
some kind of misunderstanding.

77
00:03:10,500 --> 00:03:13,291
I'm not a Protector
of the Whispering Wood.

78
00:03:13,291 --> 00:03:15,416
<i>[Arc Dragon] You are</i>
<i>the Green Ninja of legend,</i>

79
00:03:15,416 --> 00:03:18,875
<i>are you not, Lloyd,</i>
<i>son of Garmadon?</i>

80
00:03:18,875 --> 00:03:19,958
I am,

81
00:03:19,958 --> 00:03:22,458
but I've never even heard
of this place.

82
00:03:23,833 --> 00:03:25,291
<i>[roaring]</i>

83
00:03:25,291 --> 00:03:27,291
<i>Do not lie to us.</i>

84
00:03:27,291 --> 00:03:29,083
<i>You must have felt the call...</i>

85
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:31,000
<i>but you ignored it.</i>

86
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,458
<i>The first Green Ninja</i>
<i>to ever abandon their duties,</i>

87
00:03:34,458 --> 00:03:35,833
<i>to neglect the wood</i>

88
00:03:35,833 --> 00:03:39,125
<i>from which mortal Life itself</i>
<i>originally sprang forth!</i>

89
00:03:39,125 --> 00:03:41,583
There have been
other Green Ninja?

90
00:03:41,583 --> 00:03:43,166
The prophecy never said
anything about--

91
00:03:43,166 --> 00:03:45,583
<i>[Arc Dragon] Of course</i>
<i>there have been others,</i>

92
00:03:45,583 --> 00:03:48,458
<i>and each one has performed</i>
<i>the Ritual of Unrooting</i>

93
00:03:48,458 --> 00:03:50,916
<i>to maintain the power</i>
<i>of this wood,</i>

94
00:03:50,916 --> 00:03:52,416
<i>until you!</i>

95
00:03:52,416 --> 00:03:53,791
I didn't know any of this.

96
00:03:53,791 --> 00:03:55,958
I thought I'd reached
my true potential!

97
00:03:55,958 --> 00:03:59,833
<i>You believe you only have</i>
<i>one true potential?</i>

98
00:03:59,833 --> 00:04:01,333
<i>That any of us do?</i>

99
00:04:01,333 --> 00:04:02,750
Hey, go easy!

100
00:04:02,750 --> 00:04:05,541
Lloyd protected this place
as soon as he got here.

101
00:04:05,541 --> 00:04:06,666
He saved these little guys

102
00:04:06,666 --> 00:04:09,583
from some weird monster dudes!

103
00:04:10,666 --> 00:04:12,500
<i>Too little, too late.</i>

104
00:04:12,500 --> 00:04:13,916
<i>Without the Master of Life,</i>

105
00:04:13,916 --> 00:04:15,708
<i>the Whispering Wood</i>
<i>has weakened,</i>

106
00:04:15,708 --> 00:04:17,208
<i>its light dimmed.</i>

107
00:04:17,208 --> 00:04:18,583
I swear to you,

108
00:04:18,583 --> 00:04:20,583
I-I had no idea.

109
00:04:20,583 --> 00:04:23,041
<i>All the other Life Masters</i>
<i>found their way here</i>

110
00:04:23,041 --> 00:04:24,833
<i>as soon as they came of age.</i>

111
00:04:24,833 --> 00:04:26,416
"Came of age"?

112
00:04:26,416 --> 00:04:29,333
<i>A stage of maturation</i>
<i>for mortals.</i>

113
00:04:29,333 --> 00:04:31,750
<i>The transition</i>
<i>out of childhood.</i>

114
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:35,416
Oh... that must be the reason.

115
00:04:35,416 --> 00:04:36,958
When I was a kid,

116
00:04:36,958 --> 00:04:39,541
there was an incident
with Tomorrow's Tea,

117
00:04:39,541 --> 00:04:43,625
and poof,
I was instantly a teenager.

118
00:04:43,625 --> 00:04:46,500
I guess I...
never really came of age.

119
00:04:46,500 --> 00:04:47,958
[quietly] Did you know that?

120
00:04:47,958 --> 00:04:50,000
He skipped
part of his childhood?

121
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,208
[quietly] No idea.

122
00:04:51,208 --> 00:04:53,666
Gotta say, that's messed up.

123
00:04:53,666 --> 00:04:58,666
<i>I see. You say</i>
<i>your aging was... unnatural.</i>

124
00:04:58,666 --> 00:05:02,291
<i>We have been angry with you</i>
<i>for so long, Life Master.</i>

125
00:05:02,291 --> 00:05:05,875
<i>Truly, you could not have known</i>
<i>what was needed of you.</i>

126
00:05:05,875 --> 00:05:08,041
<i>We...</i>

127
00:05:08,041 --> 00:05:09,833
<i>apologize.</i>

128
00:05:09,833 --> 00:05:11,916
I never imagined my rapid aging

129
00:05:11,916 --> 00:05:14,833
would have consequences
for anyone except me.

130
00:05:14,833 --> 00:05:16,875
<i>The day you were exposed</i>
<i>to that tea</i>

131
00:05:16,875 --> 00:05:19,916
<i>was the day our fate,</i>
<i>and the fate of this wood,</i>

132
00:05:19,916 --> 00:05:22,708
<i>was sealed.</i>

133
00:05:22,708 --> 00:05:24,291
[Wyldfyre]
Are you two done yet?

134
00:05:24,291 --> 00:05:26,375
We gotta get back
to the Monastery

135
00:05:26,375 --> 00:05:28,666
and figure out
why my power's all wonky.

136
00:05:28,666 --> 00:05:30,458
Our powers
are acting weird too.

137
00:05:30,458 --> 00:05:31,916
You don't see us
worrying about it.

138
00:05:31,916 --> 00:05:35,000
[Wyldfyre]
Yeah, but my powers are cool.

139
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:36,375
If shaking the dumb ground

140
00:05:36,375 --> 00:05:37,916
or building robot vacuums

141
00:05:37,916 --> 00:05:39,375
was the only thing I could do...

142
00:05:39,375 --> 00:05:41,916
[snorting] I wouldn't
be bothered either.

143
00:05:41,916 --> 00:05:42,875
Relax.

144
00:05:42,875 --> 00:05:44,916
We've earned a vacation.

145
00:05:44,916 --> 00:05:47,000
We just stopped
an undead dragon.

146
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,625
Besides,
how would we leave here

147
00:05:49,625 --> 00:05:51,250
even if we wanted to, Wyldfyre?

148
00:05:51,250 --> 00:05:53,250
We haven't seen anyone else,

149
00:05:53,250 --> 00:05:55,625
we have no way to contact
the other Ninja...

150
00:05:55,625 --> 00:05:58,333
The other Ninja.

151
00:05:58,333 --> 00:06:02,000
Oh, wow. I really hope
everyone's okay.

152
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,500
We should probably head back.

153
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:05,458
We just need to...

154
00:06:05,458 --> 00:06:07,958
[bushes rustling]

155
00:06:07,958 --> 00:06:09,708
[sniffing]

156
00:06:09,708 --> 00:06:10,708
[growling]

157
00:06:12,833 --> 00:06:13,791
[meowing]

158
00:06:13,791 --> 00:06:16,291
[Sora] Cats?

159
00:06:16,291 --> 00:06:17,166
Yes!

160
00:06:17,166 --> 00:06:18,750
[meowing]

161
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:20,083
No, no, no, I'm allergic!

162
00:06:20,083 --> 00:06:21,041
I'll swell up
like a puffer fish!

163
00:06:21,041 --> 00:06:22,666
[meowing]

164
00:06:22,666 --> 00:06:24,375
Or...

165
00:06:24,375 --> 00:06:26,125
maybe my allergies are cured?

166
00:06:26,125 --> 00:06:29,000
-This place is purr...fect!
-[cats purring]

167
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,250
[Wyldfyre groans]

168
00:06:31,250 --> 00:06:32,916
[creature snarling]

169
00:06:35,208 --> 00:06:36,541
[Kai] I got this!

170
00:06:36,541 --> 00:06:38,625
Not our first time
facing flying creeps!

171
00:06:38,625 --> 00:06:40,625
[Jay] Why you gotta keep
rubbing it in?

172
00:06:40,625 --> 00:06:42,333
I don't remember anything!

173
00:06:44,291 --> 00:06:45,375
[power shorting out]

174
00:06:48,208 --> 00:06:49,833
-[Nya yelping]
-[Jay] Nya!

175
00:06:52,083 --> 00:06:53,416
[Jay struggles]

176
00:06:53,416 --> 00:06:55,291
[mech suit creaking]

177
00:06:57,333 --> 00:06:58,916
[grunting with effort]

178
00:06:58,916 --> 00:06:59,833
Whoa!

179
00:07:00,750 --> 00:07:03,000
[grunting with impact]

180
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,333
[Nya struggles]

181
00:07:06,500 --> 00:07:09,083
[groaning and yelping]

182
00:07:09,083 --> 00:07:11,000
Whoa! Aah!

183
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,166
[creature snarling]

184
00:07:12,166 --> 00:07:13,458
[screaming]

185
00:07:13,458 --> 00:07:15,583
[creature snarling]

186
00:07:15,583 --> 00:07:16,666
Aah!

187
00:07:16,666 --> 00:07:18,291
[♪♪♪]

188
00:07:18,291 --> 00:07:20,291
-Whoa!
-[creature splatting]

189
00:07:20,291 --> 00:07:21,291
[gasping]

190
00:07:21,291 --> 00:07:24,208
Why is this cave so... wet?

191
00:07:24,208 --> 00:07:25,166
[creatures snarling]

192
00:07:25,166 --> 00:07:26,041
[Jay gagging]

193
00:07:26,041 --> 00:07:27,416
[groaning]

194
00:07:27,416 --> 00:07:28,958
I don't think it's a cave!

195
00:07:28,958 --> 00:07:30,250
[ground rumbling]

196
00:07:30,250 --> 00:07:31,708
[Kai] What is that?

197
00:07:31,708 --> 00:07:32,666
An earthquake?

198
00:07:32,666 --> 00:07:34,708
Oh no. Grab onto something!

199
00:07:34,708 --> 00:07:35,833
Grab something?

200
00:07:35,833 --> 00:07:37,500
Do you know
how slimy everything is?

201
00:07:37,500 --> 00:07:39,125
[rumbling]

202
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:40,208
-[belching rumble]
-[Kai and Nya yelping]

203
00:07:40,208 --> 00:07:42,500
Whoa! Whoa...

204
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:44,083
[grunting with effort]

205
00:07:44,083 --> 00:07:46,208
It smells horrible.

206
00:07:46,208 --> 00:07:47,750
[grunting with effort]

207
00:07:47,750 --> 00:07:48,875
Aah!

208
00:07:48,875 --> 00:07:51,041
I can't believe
I'm about to say these words,

209
00:07:51,041 --> 00:07:54,458
but I'm pretty sure
we're in a Quealiche's stomach!

210
00:07:54,458 --> 00:07:55,958
What's a Quealiche?

211
00:07:55,958 --> 00:07:57,250
Enormous slug-like creatures

212
00:07:57,250 --> 00:07:59,166
that burrow through
the Land of Madness.

213
00:07:59,166 --> 00:08:01,750
I was briefly transferred
to the Decontamination Chamber

214
00:08:01,750 --> 00:08:03,083
in the Administration,

215
00:08:03,083 --> 00:08:05,583
and had to hose off agents
unlucky enough to run into one.

216
00:08:05,583 --> 00:08:07,333
I'd know this stench anywhere!

217
00:08:07,333 --> 00:08:08,333
[grunting with effort]

218
00:08:08,333 --> 00:08:09,541
You mean that gust of wind

219
00:08:09,541 --> 00:08:11,083
was a... belch?

220
00:08:11,083 --> 00:08:12,666
Oh, gross.

221
00:08:12,666 --> 00:08:13,958
How did the Monastery

222
00:08:13,958 --> 00:08:15,958
end up inside the belly
of a giant slug

223
00:08:15,958 --> 00:08:17,375
in the Land of Madness?

224
00:08:17,375 --> 00:08:19,583
[Kai] Bigger question,
how do we get out?

225
00:08:19,583 --> 00:08:22,166
Preferably
before we get digested.

226
00:08:22,166 --> 00:08:23,666
[Jay] Only two options,

227
00:08:23,666 --> 00:08:25,833
so I vote we find its mouth!

228
00:08:25,833 --> 00:08:26,875
Grab on!

229
00:08:28,583 --> 00:08:30,041
[♪♪♪]

230
00:08:32,166 --> 00:08:33,208
[creature snarling]

231
00:08:37,208 --> 00:08:39,208
Oh! [chuckling] Thank you.

232
00:08:39,208 --> 00:08:40,833
[♪♪♪]

233
00:08:42,166 --> 00:08:43,666
You're worried about Lloyd.

234
00:08:43,666 --> 00:08:44,875
[Arin] All this new info

235
00:08:44,875 --> 00:08:46,750
about who he's supposed to be,

236
00:08:46,750 --> 00:08:48,541
it's gotta be overwhelming.

237
00:08:48,541 --> 00:08:49,750
Like a nightmare

238
00:08:49,750 --> 00:08:52,166
where you have a test
you didn't study for.

239
00:08:52,166 --> 00:08:54,375
I wish there was
something I could do.

240
00:08:54,375 --> 00:08:57,625
Arin, you're the only one
without Elemental Powers.

241
00:08:57,625 --> 00:08:59,875
Thanks, Euphrasia. Rub it in.

242
00:08:59,875 --> 00:09:02,083
I mean, it's an advantage.

243
00:09:02,083 --> 00:09:04,208
You're the most dependable
at the moment.

244
00:09:04,208 --> 00:09:07,583
You've never had powers,
and you don't need them.

245
00:09:07,583 --> 00:09:10,708
Lloyd will rely on you now
more than ever.

246
00:09:10,708 --> 00:09:13,958
[Lloyd] This thing
you needed me to do...?

247
00:09:13,958 --> 00:09:16,041
<i>[Arc Dragon]</i>
<i>The Rite of Unrooting.</i>

248
00:09:16,041 --> 00:09:17,833
<i>It maintains the Wood.</i>

249
00:09:17,833 --> 00:09:19,583
Maintains?

250
00:09:19,583 --> 00:09:21,333
<i>[Arc Dragon]</i>
<i>All Realms are connected,</i>

251
00:09:21,333 --> 00:09:23,333
<i>even before the Merge.</i>

252
00:09:23,333 --> 00:09:25,000
<i>Like water through roots,</i>

253
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:27,333
<i>or bees spreading pollen,</i>

254
00:09:27,333 --> 00:09:30,458
<i>Source Energy flows</i>
<i>through unseen paths</i>

255
00:09:30,458 --> 00:09:33,541
<i>across every land</i>
<i>and all people.</i>

256
00:09:33,541 --> 00:09:35,333
<i>To maintain the Whispering Wood</i>

257
00:09:35,333 --> 00:09:37,500
<i>is to cleanse those pathways,</i>

258
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:40,958
<i>to sustain the connection</i>
<i>between all life.</i>

259
00:09:40,958 --> 00:09:42,125
Okay.

260
00:09:42,125 --> 00:09:44,333
I'm late, but I'm here now.

261
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:46,291
How do I perform this rite?

262
00:09:46,291 --> 00:09:48,416
<i>[Arc Dragon]</i>
<i>I wish it were possible.</i>

263
00:09:48,416 --> 00:09:50,708
<i>While the Rite teaches you</i>
<i>the truth</i>

264
00:09:50,708 --> 00:09:52,958
<i>about the Green Ninja's</i>
<i>Elemental Powers,</i>

265
00:09:52,958 --> 00:09:54,916
<i>the time has passed.</i>

266
00:09:54,916 --> 00:09:57,750
<i>One as old as you</i>
<i>would never survive it.</i>

267
00:09:57,750 --> 00:10:00,375
<i>Your roots have spread</i>
<i>too deep and too wide</i>

268
00:10:00,375 --> 00:10:02,291
<i>to change your current path.</i>

269
00:10:02,291 --> 00:10:05,125
It would teach me
the truth about my powers?

270
00:10:05,125 --> 00:10:07,208
I've never fully
understood them.

271
00:10:07,208 --> 00:10:08,791
I've been called
the Master of Power,

272
00:10:08,791 --> 00:10:10,250
the Master of Energy.

273
00:10:10,250 --> 00:10:12,458
Nothing ever really fit.

274
00:10:12,458 --> 00:10:14,916
Sometimes I didn't really fit.

275
00:10:14,916 --> 00:10:18,666
It is energy, but... what kind?

276
00:10:18,666 --> 00:10:20,375
It doesn't burn like fire,

277
00:10:20,375 --> 00:10:22,083
or shock like lightning.

278
00:10:24,208 --> 00:10:25,333
<i>[Arc Dragon]</i>
<i>Would you name a flower</i>

279
00:10:25,333 --> 00:10:26,791
<i>from the shape of its seed?</i>

280
00:10:26,791 --> 00:10:28,500
<i>Know the lean of a tree</i>

281
00:10:28,500 --> 00:10:30,375
<i>before it is planted?</i>

282
00:10:30,375 --> 00:10:32,791
<i>The mystical nature</i>
<i>of your sudden aging</i>

283
00:10:32,791 --> 00:10:34,541
<i>stunted your powers.</i>

284
00:10:34,541 --> 00:10:37,458
<i>The potential</i>
<i>has not fully blossomed.</i>

285
00:10:37,458 --> 00:10:39,250
Well, now it may never.

286
00:10:39,250 --> 00:10:41,916
Something is wrong
with all our Elemental Powers.

287
00:10:41,916 --> 00:10:43,375
<i>[Arc Dragon] I am aware.</i>

288
00:10:43,375 --> 00:10:46,000
<i>Some of the Source Dragons</i>
<i>have withdrawn their connection</i>

289
00:10:46,000 --> 00:10:47,750
<i>to the Merged Lands.</i>

290
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:49,916
<i>That's why the powers</i>
<i>of Elemental Masters</i>

291
00:10:49,916 --> 00:10:51,875
<i>are unreliable.</i>

292
00:10:51,875 --> 00:10:54,041
Wait... seriously?

293
00:10:54,041 --> 00:10:55,208
<i>[Arc Dragon] Yes.</i>

294
00:10:55,208 --> 00:10:57,916
<i>Sadly, our own Source, Life,</i>

295
00:10:57,916 --> 00:11:00,625
<i>is one of those who no longer</i>
<i>nourishes the land,</i>

296
00:11:00,625 --> 00:11:03,333
<i>and so, the decline</i>
<i>of the Whispering Wood</i>

297
00:11:03,333 --> 00:11:04,875
<i>will soon quicken.</i>

298
00:11:04,875 --> 00:11:07,000
<i>Our end is at hand.</i>

299
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:08,333
But why would--

300
00:11:08,333 --> 00:11:10,708
Oh, no. This is my fault!

301
00:11:10,708 --> 00:11:13,541
I had my team summon
the Arc Dragon of Focus.

302
00:11:13,541 --> 00:11:15,416
I was warned
it might anger them,

303
00:11:15,416 --> 00:11:17,041
but I had no choice.

304
00:11:17,041 --> 00:11:19,166
<i>[Arc Dragon]</i>
<i>Withdrawn Source energy,</i>

305
00:11:19,166 --> 00:11:21,166
<i>unbalanced elemental powers--</i>

306
00:11:21,166 --> 00:11:23,625
<i>if only the Rite</i>
<i>had been performed,</i>

307
00:11:23,625 --> 00:11:25,416
<i>the power of the Master of Life</i>

308
00:11:25,416 --> 00:11:27,500
<i>might have overcome</i>
<i>all of this.</i>

309
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,291
All my life,

310
00:11:29,291 --> 00:11:32,500
I've been pushed
in so many directions...

311
00:11:32,500 --> 00:11:35,666
prophecies, destiny, visions.

312
00:11:35,666 --> 00:11:38,000
I can't always tell
what I'm choosing to do

313
00:11:38,000 --> 00:11:41,000
or what fate
is forcing me to do,

314
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:42,916
but if there's even a chance

315
00:11:42,916 --> 00:11:44,500
to stabilize Source Energy

316
00:11:44,500 --> 00:11:45,708
while saving this wood,

317
00:11:45,708 --> 00:11:48,416
then I choose to take that risk.

318
00:11:53,041 --> 00:11:54,666
[Kai] It's not smelling
any better.

319
00:11:54,666 --> 00:11:57,583
[Nya grunts with effort]

320
00:11:57,583 --> 00:11:59,500
[Kai] Pretty sure this is
the way to the mouth.

321
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:01,208
[tendrils slapping]

322
00:12:02,541 --> 00:12:03,958
[Kai] We're not gonna make it!

323
00:12:03,958 --> 00:12:05,041
[Jay] Oh, yes, we are.

324
00:12:05,041 --> 00:12:06,666
Nya, flood the stomach.

325
00:12:06,666 --> 00:12:08,083
Kai, turn up the heat.

326
00:12:08,083 --> 00:12:10,583
A little heartburn is just
what the doctor ordered.

327
00:12:10,583 --> 00:12:12,458
[Nya grunts with effort]

328
00:12:12,458 --> 00:12:13,791
H'yah!

329
00:12:15,333 --> 00:12:16,875
[creatures screeching]

330
00:12:16,875 --> 00:12:18,583
[Kai grunting with effort]

331
00:12:18,583 --> 00:12:20,500
Oh, man, not now.

332
00:12:20,500 --> 00:12:23,416
[Jay groaning] I was hoping
it wouldn't come to this.

333
00:12:23,416 --> 00:12:25,583
-[beeping remote]
-Goodbye, my friend.

334
00:12:25,583 --> 00:12:27,041
[Kai] Which one of us
is he talking to?

335
00:12:27,041 --> 00:12:28,083
-Ah!
-[Nya gasping]

336
00:12:28,083 --> 00:12:29,166
[countdown timer beeping]

337
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:33,875
[countdown beeping accelerating]

338
00:12:36,250 --> 00:12:38,166
[explosion]

339
00:12:40,708 --> 00:12:42,750
[Nya] Sorry.
I know you loved that thing.

340
00:12:42,750 --> 00:12:43,791
[Jay sighs]

341
00:12:43,791 --> 00:12:46,208
Guess I love living more.

342
00:12:46,208 --> 00:12:47,625
[deep rumbling]

343
00:12:47,625 --> 00:12:48,791
[gurgling belch]

344
00:12:48,791 --> 00:12:49,708
[Jay] It worked!

345
00:12:49,708 --> 00:12:51,208
Get ready for it.

346
00:12:51,208 --> 00:12:52,750
[Kai] Get ready for what?
Get ready for what?!

347
00:12:52,750 --> 00:12:54,541
[thundering wave,
all screaming]

348
00:12:54,541 --> 00:12:57,250
[dragons snoring]

349
00:12:57,250 --> 00:12:59,541
[ground rumbling]

350
00:13:01,375 --> 00:13:03,125
[rumbling]

351
00:13:03,125 --> 00:13:05,250
[explosive roaring]

352
00:13:06,250 --> 00:13:07,541
[gurgling and bellowing]

353
00:13:08,833 --> 00:13:09,958
[vomiting]

354
00:13:09,958 --> 00:13:12,916
[screaming]

355
00:13:14,666 --> 00:13:15,833
[grunting with impact]

356
00:13:15,833 --> 00:13:17,625
[Nya gasps] Ew!

357
00:13:17,625 --> 00:13:19,500
I can't believe that worked!

358
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:20,750
[Kai groans]

359
00:13:21,833 --> 00:13:23,166
I forgot how messy

360
00:13:23,166 --> 00:13:24,958
hanging out with you
could be, Jay.

361
00:13:24,958 --> 00:13:26,916
[Jay] Don't anyone
celebrate too soon.

362
00:13:27,833 --> 00:13:28,833
[growling]

363
00:13:28,833 --> 00:13:29,791
[Kai]
These aren't the same dragons

364
00:13:29,791 --> 00:13:31,166
we ran into last time, are they?

365
00:13:31,166 --> 00:13:32,208
[Nya] They are,

366
00:13:32,208 --> 00:13:34,250
and they're not happy
we woke them up.

367
00:13:34,250 --> 00:13:35,541
[roaring]

368
00:13:38,416 --> 00:13:40,791
How am I
supposed to guide us out

369
00:13:40,791 --> 00:13:43,041
when it's dawn
in every direction?

370
00:13:43,041 --> 00:13:44,625
[Sora] Maybe we're not
supposed to leave.

371
00:13:44,625 --> 00:13:46,750
Where'd those cats
even come from?

372
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:48,291
-Why does that matter?
-[cats purring]

373
00:13:48,291 --> 00:13:50,750
Can't you just
enjoy something for once?

374
00:13:50,750 --> 00:13:52,708
[gasping in delight]

375
00:13:52,708 --> 00:13:54,208
Pie!

376
00:13:55,666 --> 00:13:57,000
[munching]

377
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,625
Hmm. They're a little cold.

378
00:13:59,625 --> 00:14:01,458
Huh...

379
00:14:01,458 --> 00:14:03,500
That wasn't there a second ago.

380
00:14:03,500 --> 00:14:05,416
but I'm glad it's here now!

381
00:14:05,416 --> 00:14:06,708
You guys
don't think it's strange

382
00:14:06,708 --> 00:14:09,458
your favorite thing is pies,
and then there's pies?

383
00:14:09,458 --> 00:14:11,500
And your favorite thing is cats,

384
00:14:11,500 --> 00:14:13,125
and then there's cats?

385
00:14:13,125 --> 00:14:15,083
[Riyu grumbles]

386
00:14:15,083 --> 00:14:16,916
[cats meowing]

387
00:14:17,916 --> 00:14:19,083
-[Sora] No.
-[Frak] No.

388
00:14:19,083 --> 00:14:21,541
Ah! Pies are not supposed
to grow on bushes!

389
00:14:21,541 --> 00:14:24,250
Wyldmelons can't grow
outside the Wyldness!

390
00:14:24,250 --> 00:14:26,916
This place is full of trickery!

391
00:14:26,916 --> 00:14:29,000
[panting angrily]

392
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,166
[sniffing]

393
00:14:31,166 --> 00:14:32,791
[grumbling curiously]

394
00:14:32,791 --> 00:14:34,208
[sniffing]

395
00:14:34,208 --> 00:14:35,500
[grumbling]

396
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:36,916
You got a scent?

397
00:14:36,916 --> 00:14:38,541
[grumbling language]

398
00:14:38,541 --> 00:14:40,916
An unusual scent?

399
00:14:40,916 --> 00:14:42,875
-Maybe it's a way out of here.
-Whoa!

400
00:14:42,875 --> 00:14:44,541
Let's go.

401
00:14:44,541 --> 00:14:46,375
[Sora groans in disappointment]

402
00:14:46,375 --> 00:14:48,666
-[cats meowing]
-Oh...

403
00:14:49,875 --> 00:14:50,958
[cats meowing]

404
00:14:53,833 --> 00:14:55,125
[Jay] Even
in the middle of nowhere,

405
00:14:55,125 --> 00:14:56,625
you two have enemies?

406
00:14:56,625 --> 00:14:58,250
[grunting in combat]

407
00:14:58,250 --> 00:15:00,750
[Jay] Why am I hanging out
with you people?

408
00:15:00,750 --> 00:15:01,666
[dragons grunting]

409
00:15:01,666 --> 00:15:03,708
[suit damage alert beeping]

410
00:15:03,708 --> 00:15:04,875
[♪♪♪]

411
00:15:06,750 --> 00:15:08,708
[countdown timer beeping]

412
00:15:08,708 --> 00:15:11,416
[Kai] Buddy, you're running out
of things to blow up.

413
00:15:11,416 --> 00:15:12,833
[countdown timer accelerating]

414
00:15:16,500 --> 00:15:17,375
Whoa!

415
00:15:27,125 --> 00:15:28,166
[Kai] Come on!

416
00:15:29,208 --> 00:15:30,250
[Nya] Wait!

417
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:32,000
[dragons snarling]

418
00:15:32,000 --> 00:15:33,083
[Jay gasps]

419
00:15:36,458 --> 00:15:38,833
[Jay] I can't do Spinjitzu!
I can't do Spinjitzu!

420
00:15:38,833 --> 00:15:40,666
[panicked voice echoing]

421
00:15:40,666 --> 00:15:42,083
[gasping]

422
00:15:42,083 --> 00:15:43,750
[roaring]

423
00:15:48,375 --> 00:15:49,541
[dragon squeaking]

424
00:15:50,541 --> 00:15:51,750
[dragon roaring]

425
00:15:53,083 --> 00:15:55,083
[Jay] I'm fine!

426
00:15:55,083 --> 00:15:56,583
-[Kai] Over-under!
-[Jay] What-what?

427
00:15:56,583 --> 00:15:58,458
[roaring]

428
00:15:58,458 --> 00:16:00,000
[Kai] It's what it sounds like.

429
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,333
[Jay yelping, dragon roaring]

430
00:16:03,750 --> 00:16:05,166
[Kai] H'yah! H'up!

431
00:16:05,166 --> 00:16:06,125
[dragon roaring]

432
00:16:06,125 --> 00:16:07,208
H'yah!

433
00:16:08,125 --> 00:16:09,125
[Nya] What now?

434
00:16:09,125 --> 00:16:10,458
[Kai] You could try apologizing.

435
00:16:10,458 --> 00:16:11,375
[Nya] Me?

436
00:16:11,375 --> 00:16:13,166
They literally chased you!

437
00:16:13,166 --> 00:16:15,250
[Kai] Let's use their anger
against them.

438
00:16:16,458 --> 00:16:18,500
[Nya] Hey, dirt-eater!

439
00:16:18,500 --> 00:16:21,375
I've seen bigger horns
on a tricycle!

440
00:16:21,375 --> 00:16:23,041
[Kai] Earth Dragon?

441
00:16:23,041 --> 00:16:24,916
More like Barf Dragon!

442
00:16:24,916 --> 00:16:26,708
[roaring]

443
00:16:26,708 --> 00:16:27,666
[grunting with effort]

444
00:16:31,708 --> 00:16:34,083
[roaring]

445
00:16:34,083 --> 00:16:35,250
[laughing]

446
00:16:35,250 --> 00:16:36,875
Man, that felt good!

447
00:16:36,875 --> 00:16:38,750
Working like that
jog any memories, Jay?

448
00:16:38,750 --> 00:16:40,000
No!

449
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,250
You two share a look

450
00:16:41,250 --> 00:16:42,958
and know what
the other's thinking.

451
00:16:42,958 --> 00:16:45,208
I can't even remember
how to do Spinjitzu,

452
00:16:45,208 --> 00:16:46,791
which seems like
the bare minimum

453
00:16:46,791 --> 00:16:48,541
to call yourself a Ninja.

454
00:16:48,541 --> 00:16:51,041
Even that kid
with no powers can do it.

455
00:16:51,041 --> 00:16:52,500
That's what training's for.

456
00:16:52,500 --> 00:16:53,916
Even we have to train.

457
00:16:53,916 --> 00:16:55,708
There's always room to grow.

458
00:16:55,708 --> 00:16:57,833
[sighing] You don't get it.

459
00:16:57,833 --> 00:17:00,541
I hated working
for the Administration.

460
00:17:00,541 --> 00:17:02,750
I lost in the Tournament
of Sources.

461
00:17:02,750 --> 00:17:05,666
I was only a pretty good
bounty hunter.

462
00:17:05,666 --> 00:17:06,583
So?

463
00:17:06,583 --> 00:17:09,666
So? No more failures.

464
00:17:09,666 --> 00:17:11,333
If I'm gonna be a Ninja,

465
00:17:11,333 --> 00:17:13,250
I need to be a great one.

466
00:17:13,250 --> 00:17:14,416
It's another reason

467
00:17:14,416 --> 00:17:17,125
I need to remember
my forgotten memories.

468
00:17:17,125 --> 00:17:19,083
I don't know how,

469
00:17:19,083 --> 00:17:21,333
I don't know
if it's even possible,

470
00:17:21,333 --> 00:17:22,791
but I have to.

471
00:17:22,791 --> 00:17:24,041
We'll help you.

472
00:17:28,875 --> 00:17:29,833
Whoa...

473
00:17:35,291 --> 00:17:37,375
[Wyldfyre] What is this thing?

474
00:17:37,375 --> 00:17:41,041
[Sora] Actually...
I have no idea.

475
00:17:43,166 --> 00:17:45,291
It's definitely not normal.

476
00:17:45,291 --> 00:17:46,541
Well, in we go.

477
00:17:46,541 --> 00:17:47,708
Whoa!

478
00:17:47,708 --> 00:17:49,625
I'm not jumping into
some mystery black hole

479
00:17:49,625 --> 00:17:51,041
just cause you said so.

480
00:17:51,041 --> 00:17:52,375
I agree with Frak.

481
00:17:52,375 --> 00:17:54,208
There's no rush
to leave this place.

482
00:17:54,208 --> 00:17:55,875
It has everything we need.

483
00:17:55,875 --> 00:17:58,250
Yeah, which isn't normal.

484
00:17:58,250 --> 00:17:59,875
It has to be a trap!

485
00:17:59,875 --> 00:18:01,750
It wants us to stay here forever!

486
00:18:02,625 --> 00:18:04,708
No, that's a trap.

487
00:18:04,708 --> 00:18:05,958
Totally.

488
00:18:05,958 --> 00:18:07,291
Now, where was that pie bush?

489
00:18:07,291 --> 00:18:10,583
The pie bush is a trap,
you clown-faces!

490
00:18:10,583 --> 00:18:12,916
Don't you see what this place
is doing to you?

491
00:18:13,833 --> 00:18:14,750
[together] No.

492
00:18:15,666 --> 00:18:18,583
[sighing]
This is for your own good.

493
00:18:18,583 --> 00:18:19,541
[shrieking] Yaah!

494
00:18:20,708 --> 00:18:22,875
-Whoa!
-Wha...!

495
00:18:25,916 --> 00:18:26,916
[gasping]

496
00:18:27,958 --> 00:18:28,916
Perfect!

497
00:18:32,291 --> 00:18:33,541
[Frak wails]

498
00:18:34,666 --> 00:18:37,333
You're the one who's not
in her right mind, Wyldfyre.

499
00:18:37,333 --> 00:18:38,833
[Frak] You should really
listen to us.

500
00:18:39,791 --> 00:18:40,833
Hold on.

501
00:18:40,833 --> 00:18:43,250
Take a deep breath
and calm down.

502
00:18:43,250 --> 00:18:46,875
You don't get to tell me
to calm down!

503
00:18:46,875 --> 00:18:47,916
[roaring]

504
00:18:49,958 --> 00:18:51,708
[grunting in combat]

505
00:18:55,083 --> 00:18:56,333
[groaning]

506
00:18:58,625 --> 00:18:59,541
[grunting in combat]

507
00:19:05,875 --> 00:19:07,083
[roaring]

508
00:19:07,083 --> 00:19:08,083
[grunting with effort]

509
00:19:12,791 --> 00:19:14,375
Why are you smiling?

510
00:19:14,375 --> 00:19:15,333
We have you beat.

511
00:19:15,333 --> 00:19:17,166
Aw... you two teamed up.

512
00:19:17,166 --> 00:19:18,166
Cute,

513
00:19:18,166 --> 00:19:20,958
but I always team up
with dragons.

514
00:19:20,958 --> 00:19:21,958
[roaring]

515
00:19:21,958 --> 00:19:23,416
Ah!

516
00:19:23,416 --> 00:19:26,666
[all wailing]

517
00:19:26,666 --> 00:19:28,625
<i>[Arc Dragon] Deep within</i>
<i>the Whispering Wood</i>

518
00:19:28,625 --> 00:19:30,708
<i>is the Temple</i>
<i>of the Green Ninja.</i>

519
00:19:30,708 --> 00:19:32,250
<i>Inside, you will be guided</i>

520
00:19:32,250 --> 00:19:34,666
<i>to perform</i>
<i>the Rite of Unrooting.</i>

521
00:19:34,666 --> 00:19:35,916
<i>The temple is hidden,</i>

522
00:19:35,916 --> 00:19:39,041
<i>even from the eyes and ears</i>
<i>of the forest.</i>

523
00:19:39,041 --> 00:19:41,000
[Lloyd] Then...
how will we find it?

524
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,375
<i>[Arc Dragon]</i>
<i>If you are meant to,</i>

525
00:19:42,375 --> 00:19:43,875
<i>it will call to you,</i>

526
00:19:43,875 --> 00:19:46,083
<i>but I must warn you again,</i>

527
00:19:46,083 --> 00:19:48,583
<i>the journey on which</i>
<i>you are about to embark</i>

528
00:19:48,583 --> 00:19:50,416
<i>will be treacherous.</i>

529
00:19:50,416 --> 00:19:52,708
That's not enough to stop me.

530
00:20:00,125 --> 00:20:02,833
[♪♪♪]

531
00:20:05,666 --> 00:20:07,916
[wailing]

532
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:10,625
[grunting with impact]

533
00:20:10,625 --> 00:20:11,625
Ah!

534
00:20:12,583 --> 00:20:15,750
Welcome to Umbrasilvis.

535
00:20:16,833 --> 00:20:19,500
Wait a second...

536
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:21,416
pies don't grow on bushes!

537
00:20:21,416 --> 00:20:23,875
And where did
those cats come from?

538
00:20:23,875 --> 00:20:26,500
[sighing] I...
I don't know what came over us.

539
00:20:26,500 --> 00:20:27,791
[sighing]

540
00:20:27,791 --> 00:20:30,500
There was something
seriously off about that place.

541
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:32,166
Thanks for guiding us out.

542
00:20:32,166 --> 00:20:34,416
I guess you do make
a pretty good leader.

543
00:20:34,416 --> 00:20:37,083
My dragon heritage
probably made me immune

544
00:20:37,083 --> 00:20:39,083
to whatever got into your heads.

545
00:20:39,083 --> 00:20:41,375
Riyu wasn't affected either.

546
00:20:41,375 --> 00:20:43,791
I may have heroically
gotten us out of there,

547
00:20:43,791 --> 00:20:44,750
which some might say

548
00:20:44,750 --> 00:20:46,708
is the most heroic thing
ever done.

549
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:48,666
[sighing]

550
00:20:48,666 --> 00:20:50,166
But where are we now?

551
00:20:52,583 --> 00:20:55,125
[doors slamming]

552
00:20:55,125 --> 00:20:57,250
[Frak] Friendly place.

553
00:20:57,250 --> 00:20:58,375
[Sora] Look, over there.

554
00:20:58,375 --> 00:21:00,958
[♪♪♪]

555
00:21:03,083 --> 00:21:04,833
Maybe we can hitch a ride
back to Ninjago

556
00:21:04,833 --> 00:21:06,083
on that airship.

557
00:21:06,083 --> 00:21:09,041
That's an Explorer's Club ship.

558
00:21:09,041 --> 00:21:11,375
They're probably in the middle
of an important expedition.

559
00:21:11,375 --> 00:21:12,416
Too busy to help.

560
00:21:12,416 --> 00:21:13,416
Let's find another way home.

561
00:21:13,416 --> 00:21:14,833
I'm sure this place has tons

562
00:21:14,833 --> 00:21:15,791
of public transportation options.

563
00:21:15,791 --> 00:21:18,166
[slamming doors]

564
00:21:19,041 --> 00:21:23,166
[♪♪♪]

565
00:21:28,916 --> 00:21:33,166
I, uh, think I dropped
something back by the well.

566
00:21:33,166 --> 00:21:35,041
Is everything okay?

567
00:21:35,041 --> 00:21:37,083
[voice] Frak, is that you?

568
00:21:38,333 --> 00:21:40,416
[muttering]
Doesn't he look like--

569
00:21:40,416 --> 00:21:41,500
[sighing awkwardly]

570
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:42,500
Hi, Dad.

571
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:46,791
[♪♪♪]

